{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he moved on from there, etc.</b> It did not specify what he moved. And Rashi, may his memory be for blessing, explained 'his tent,' but it is lacking [that word]. Perhaps, however, he alluded that he moved the Rock from the place where He had appeared to him there — and this is what they, may their memory be for blessing, said in Berakhot (5:) on the verse (Job 18:4) ״הַלְמַעַנְךָ תֵּעָזַב אָרֶץ וְיֶעְתַּק צוּר מִמְּקוֹמוֹ״ — for when Israel departs from the place of their prayer, it causes the Rock, which is the Holy One, blessed be He, to move from His place. How much more so in what stands before us, where HaShem appeared to him and he built an altar there — so when Abraham passes on from there, the Rock will move from His place, and it is Abraham who does the moving." "<b>Further,</b> it intends that he moved the altar that he had built there: when he wished to pitch his tent in another place, he dismantled the altar he had built and rebuilt it in the place where he pitched his tent. And there was no need to spell this out, for he relied on what is stated in the adjacent verse: ״וַיִּבֶן שָׁם מִזְבֵּחַ, etc., וַיַּעְתֵּק מִשָּׁם״. He also pointed to it with a finger by saying 'from there' — which refers back to what was stated in the adjacent passage. Understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The Talmudic source is Berakhot 6a (printed as ו: in Vilna pagination); the text reads ה: which may reflect a different edition or a typographical error."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:50.606651884Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}